OL,3,GNEWSARiding instructor returns to work
OL,4,Aafter paralysis
OL,5,
OL,6,FA retired riding instructor who was
OL,7,Fleft paralysed after she was thrown off
OL,8,Fa horse and broke her neck has returned
OL,9,Fto coaching and judging dressage.
OL,11,FSandra Jones, 66, who lives on
OL,12,FDartmoor, Devon, said the last 18
OL,13,Fmonths had been "a nightmare of
OL,14,Fadjusting to life as a quadriplegic"
OL,15,Fbut she had set herself the goal of
OL,16,Freturning to her work.
OL,18,FShe broke her neck, back and spinal
OL,19,Fcord in the accident and medics told
OL,20,Fher she may not be able to move again.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,346,340,200,160,0,100
